      "retrieved": "2026-09-26",
      "notes": "Columns: base input, 5m cache writes, 1h cache writes, cache hits, output. 'Claude 4.6 and later models ... include the full 1M token context window at standard pricing', so no long-context tier. Thinking tokens are billed as output tokens (https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/thinking). Model ids from https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/model-deprecations."
    },
    "openai": {
      "url": "https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing",
      "retrieved": "2026-09-26",
      "notes": "Standard pricing, short-context columns; long-context tier applies to prompts over 272K input tokens. Cache writes: GPT-5.6 and later 1.25x the uncached input rate; earlier models have 'No additional cache-write charge', so their cache_write_per_1m equals input_per_1m (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/prompt-caching). Reasoning tokens are 'billed as output tokens' (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/reasoning). gpt-5.6-sol is a promotional price 'available at least through November 21, 2026'."
    },
    "gemini": {
      "url": "https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing",
      "retrieved": "2026-09-26",
      "notes": "Paid tier, Standard, text/image/video input. Output price is 'including thinking tokens'. Context caching price is the cached-input rate; hourly cache storage is not per-token and is not modeled, and there is no per-token cache-write price, so rows with cache writes on Gemini models are reported unpriced. Long-context tier applies to prompts over 200k tokens. gemini-3.8-flash prices apply through December 31, 2026 and double on January 1, 2027."
    }
